💡 **SUGGESTION: a confirming endpoint report still leaves the window "unverified"**

`_applyDetectedContextWindow` publishes into the registry only when `detected != model.contextWindow`. When the endpoint's report CONFIRMS the carried catalog value (the common case for well-catalogued models), nothing is published, so `registry.isVerified(model)` stays false and the AC6 badge on every `task_status` pressure row marks that window unverified — even though the provider just verified it.

Since `publish` with the same value is a behavioral no-op (`windowFor` returns what the model already carries) and `withRegisteredContextWindow` short-circuits on `registered == model.contextWindow`, publishing unconditionally is free and makes the verification ladder honest:

```dart
if (detected != null) {
  _replaceModelLimits(
    contextWindow: detected == model.contextWindow ? null : detected,
    windowSource: ContextWindowSource.endpointReport,
  );
  ...
}
```

(with the publish reading `detected` rather than the rebuilt window, or by moving the publish next to the `detected != null` check). Purely a truth-in-UI fix; no behavior change.

# Thread 4 — a confirming endpoint report still leaves the window "unverified" (`lib/src/cli/provider_models.dart`)

Fixed exactly as suggested.

**Commit** `b5f0ff7460` — `_applyDetectedContextWindow` now treats the three cases separately:

```dart
if (detected != model.contextWindow) {
  _replaceModelLimits(contextWindow: detected, windowSource: endpointReport);
  io.writeln(_style.dim('model context window: $detected (from endpoint)'));
} else {
  // The endpoint CONFIRMED the carried value: publish it so the AC6
  // verification ladder is honest (windowFor returns what the model
  // already carries — a behavioral no-op, but isVerified flips true).
  contextWindowRegistry.publish(
    model: model,
    window: detected,
    source: ContextWindowSource.endpointReport,
  );
}
```

The confirming path publishes unconditionally into the registry — `windowFor` returns the value
the model already carries and `withRegisteredContextWindow` short-circuits on equality, so the only
observable change is `registry.isVerified(model)` → true and the `task_status` pressure badge
marking the window verified. No "(from endpoint)" dim line is printed for a confirmation (nothing
changed, so nothing to announce).

**Test** (`test/cli/copilot_provider_test.dart`): "an endpoint-reported context window in roles
mode — a CONFIRMING report verifies the registry window" drives a fetch whose reported window
equals the carried one and asserts `contextWindowRegistry.isVerified(model)` is true afterwards.
